# Category, tag and pagination addresses, by shape rather than one by one. Consulted only after
# legacy-redirects.map misses, which is what lets /categorias/android reach its alias instead of
# being swallowed here.
#
# The capture is named because $1 does not survive inside an nginx map. scripts/preview.mjs reads
# the same file and rewrites $name to $<name> for JavaScript.

~^/categorias$              https://legacy.valney.dev/blog/categorias;
~^/categorias/(?<cat>.+)$   https://legacy.valney.dev/blog/categorias/$cat;
~^/tags$                    https://legacy.valney.dev/blog/tags;
~^/tags/(?<tag>.+)$         https://legacy.valney.dev/blog/tags/$tag;
~^/page/[0-9]+$             https://legacy.valney.dev/;

# The document also listed ^/?$ to the archive root. It is deliberately absent: this domain's root
# is the site you are looking at, and that rule would send every visitor to the old blog.
